        ":question/id": "f44bdacc-ce0f-51ba-a591-548eea94148e",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "$\\int (8 x - 8)\\operatorname{sin}(5 x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (8 x - 8)\\operatorname{sin}(5 x)\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=8 x - 8\\, & \u27f9\\,{u}^{\u2032}=8 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=\\operatorname{sin}(5 x)\\, & \u27f9\\,v=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(5 x)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (8 x - 8)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}(5 x)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ (8 x - 8)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(5 x)}{5})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(5 x)}{5})\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int (8 x - 8)\\operatorname{sin}(5 x)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ -\\frac{(8 x - 8)\\operatorname{cos}(5 x)}{5}+\\frac{8\\int \\operatorname{cos}(5 x)\\,\\text{d}x}{5} \\\\ =-\\frac{(8 x - 8)\\operatorname{cos}(5 x)}{5}+\\frac{8\\operatorname{sin}(5 x)}{25}+C\\end{gathered}\n$$",
