      "question": {
        ":question/id": "43fad8bc-1c54-5faf-965a-53b37f344521",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate  $\\int 10 x\\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 10 x\\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10 x\\, & \u27f9\\,{u}^{\u2032}=10 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=\\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)\\, & \u27f9\\,v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10 x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ 10 x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)}{5}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)}{5}\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int 10 x\\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ \\frac{10 x\\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)}{5}-2\\int \\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ =\\frac{10 x\\operatorname{sin}(5 x + 8)}{5}+\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}(5 x + 8)}{5}+C\\end{gathered}\n$$",
