        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int 10 x\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 8)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 10 x\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 8)\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=10 x\\, & \u27f9\\,{u}^{\u2032}=10 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 8)\\, & \u27f9\\,v=-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 10 x\\cdot \\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 8)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ 10 x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8))\\cdot 10\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ =-10 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8)+10\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(x - 8)}{\\operatorname{sin}(x - 8)}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}(x - 8),$ where $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}(x - 8)\\,\\text{d}x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int 10 x\\operatorname{csc}^{2}(x - 8)\\,\\text{d}x= \\\\ -10 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8)+10\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}(x - 8)}{\\operatorname{sin}(x - 8)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ =-10 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8)+10\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ =-10 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8)+10\\ln|u|+C \\\\ =-10 x\\operatorname{cot}(x - 8)+10\\ln|\\operatorname{sin}(x - 8)|+C\\end{gathered}\n$$",
